    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Romosozumab, a monoclonal antibody against sclerostin, has antiresorptive and anabolic effects; it raises hip and spine bone density and reduces fractures in postmenopausal women."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "For severe osteoporosis, especially older, frail patients and those at risk of falling, or a fracture despite adequate antiresorptive therapy; monthly subcutaneous injection for 1 year, then an antiresorptive (eg, alendronate or denosumab) to prevent rapid bone loss."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Boxed warning: increased MI, stroke and cardiovascular death; don't start within 12 months of an MI or stroke."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
